; ⛔ Do NOT copy the camera basis out of scenes/main.tscn. It is STALE: the
; camera there carries `fixed_camera.gd`, which overwrites `rotation` in
; `_ready()` from its pitch/yaw exports, so whatever basis the scene file
; stores is never used and need not be correct. Copied verbatim onto a camera
; with no script it aimed 25 degrees ABOVE the horizon and this test rendered
; nothing but sky. Stating pitch and yaw outright is both correct and legible.
[node name="Camera3D" type="Camera3D" parent="."]
position = Vector3(8.66, 10, 15)
rotation = Vector3(-0.5235988, 0.5235988, 0)
projection = 1
current = true
size = 4.6
far = 120.0

